<% @title = "About" %>

<%# The ids whybother_them, reporting and reporting_unavailable are linked to
    from core. Legacy #reporting_unavailable links land at the contact advice. %>
<%= page_band "About #{site_name}" %>
<%= render :partial => 'sidebar' %>

<div id="left_column_flip" class="left_column_flip">

  <dl>
    <dt id="purpose">What is this site? <a href="#purpose" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>This is a demonstration. The authorities, people, requests, replies
        and documents on it are all invented, to show what the software does.
        Nothing here was sent to a real public body.</p>
      <p>On a real site, this page says who runs it and why.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="premise">How does it work? <a href="#premise" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>A request is written on this site and sent to the authority by
        email. Each request has its own reply address, so the authority's
        answers arrive here and are filed with the request.</p>
      <p>Requests and their correspondence are private: only the requester
        and the site's administrators can read them. A document from a reply
        becomes public only when an administrator has checked it and its
        details and published it.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="selection">Is every request published? <a href="#selection" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>No. Request threads stay private. Publishing a document makes that
        document and its details public, and nothing else from the request.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="statuses">What do the statuses mean? <a href="#statuses" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Every request has a status, shown as a mark and a name.</p>
      <ul class="status-key">
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_successful"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('successful') %></strong>
          The authority supplied everything that was asked for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_partially_successful"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('partially_successful') %></strong>
          The authority supplied part of what was asked for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_rejected"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('rejected') %></strong>
          The authority released nothing, whether because it refused the
          request or because it said it doesn't hold the information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_waiting_response"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('waiting_response') %></strong>
          The request has been sent and hasn't been answered yet. It's marked
          overdue after <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_late_after_days %>
          working days and long overdue after
          <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_very_late_after_days %>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_waiting_classification"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('waiting_classification') %></strong>
          A reply has arrived and hasn't been read and given a status yet.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_internal_review"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('internal_review') %></strong>
          The requester has asked the authority to look again at its answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <i class="icon-standalone icon_under_appeal"></i>
          <strong><%= InfoRequest.get_status_description('under_appeal') %></strong>
          The requester has appealed to the regulator or a tribunal.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </dd>

    <dt id="whybother_them">Why does a public authority have to reply? <a href="#whybother_them" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Freedom of Information law gives anyone the right to ask a public
        authority for recorded information that it holds. The authority must
        answer, normally within <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_late_after_days %>
        working days, either by providing the information or by explaining
        why the law lets it refuse.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="reuse">Can I quote or link to what is published here? <a href="#reuse" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>You can link to any published document. An authority's documents
        remain its own work: releasing them under Freedom of Information law
        doesn't by itself give permission to republish them.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="reporting"><span id="reporting_unavailable"></span>What if something here should not be published? <a href="#reporting" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Tell the people who run the site through the
        <a href="<%= help_contact_path %>">contact page</a>. Say which
        document, and what the problem is.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="who">What software does it use? <a href="#who" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p><a href="https://alaveteli.org">Alaveteli</a>, free software for
        running Freedom of Information sites.
        <a href="<%= help_alaveteli_path %>">More about the software</a>.</p>
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <div id="hash_link_padding"></div>
</div>
